The upright S13 options (4, 7) improve NHR to about -0.37 but have lower LLC (0.345), worse LFR and GDS, and leave only one or two S16 poses. Upright S16 (2) has NHR -0.419 and IWR 0.405 but GDS 0, LLC 0.172 and LFR -0.171; it leaves three S6 and two S13 poses. Upright S6 (3) has GDS 1.0 but NHR -0.949, IWR 0.276, LLC 0.172 and the worst LFR (-0.269), leaving three S16 and two S13 poses. Candidate 6 offers the best combined interlocking, stability, density and future flexibility despite its height cost."}}

